+Run the wire checks with `cargo build --locked -p archy-mcp -p archy-cli`, followed by `python3 crates/archy-mcp/tests/stdio_contract.py`, `python3 crates/archy-mcp/tests/parse_errors.py`, `python3 crates/archy-mcp/tests/compare_stdio.py`, and `python3 crates/archy-mcp/tests/mutations.py`. All four scripts honor `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` and run from the CI schema checker. `cargo test --locked -p archy-mcp` tests transport guards and writer backpressure. If Node.js is available, `node crates/archy-mcp/tests/unicode_regex.js` also checks the patterns in an ECMAScript UTF-16 regex engine.
